  "steps": [
    "To a bowl add 1 cup makhana / foxnuts (30g), dry roasted, 10 almonds (soaked in hot water for 10 minutes so it’s easy to peel), 10 cashews, 10 strands kesar / saffron, ½ tsp cardamom powder, 300ml warm milk.",
    "Soak everything together for 10–20 minutes.",
    "In the meantime, prepare a mixed fruit bowl with fruits of your choice. I used blueberries, strawberries, banana, kiwi, pomegranate and grapes - 350g in total, roughly equally divided.",
    "Once the makhana mixture has soaked, transfer it to a blender.",
    "Add 2 tbsp honey and blend until completely smooth and creamy.",
    "Pour the blended custard mixture over the fruits and mix well.",
    "Refrigerate for at least 1 hour, and your healthy, chilled fruit custard is ready to serve!"
  ],
